coder › Implemented `toc(markdown)` in `src/toc.ts` and added tests in `src/toc.test.ts`.

What changed
- `src/toc.ts`
  - Parses the document line by line (splitting on `\r?\n`, so CRLF works).
  - Tracks ``` fences: any line starting with ``` toggles in/out of a fenced code block; an unclosed fence runs to end of document.
  - Recognizes ATX headings with `/^(#{1,6}) (.*)$/` — one to six `#` followed by a space, at the start of the line.
  - `text` is the part after the `#` marks with surrounding whitespace removed.
  - `slug` is lowercase, runs of non-`a-z0-9` characters collapsed to a single `-`, and dashes trimmed from both ends.
  - Repeated slugs get `-2`, `-3`, … appended; the suffix skips forward if that candidate is already taken by another heading.
- `src/toc.test.ts`
  - 10 tests covering: no headings, all six levels, `#` count > 6 ignored, missing space after `#` ignored, text trimming, slug construction (punctuation, digits, duplicate dashes, leading/trailing dashes), `-2`/`-3` dedup, suffix collision, fenced code blocks, and unclosed fences.

Checks
- `bun test`:
  ```
  bun test v1.3.14 (0d9b296a)

   10 pass
   0 fail
   10 expect() calls
  Ran 10 tests across 1 file. [14.00ms]
  ```
- There is no typecheck/lint script in `package.json` (`bun tsc` confirms no such script).

Decisions not stated in the plan
- Interpreted “letters or digits” as ASCII `a-z0-9` after lowercasing, not Unicode letters.
- Fences are toggled by any line starting with ``` (so ```js info strings and unclosed fences behave predictably).
- Headings must be at the start of the line (no leading whitespace).

Committed on `work/main` as two commits: implementation, then tests.

